{"title":"1958 AHSME Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1958_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of a circle is doubled when its radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> equals:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/8753ef6119c931a6ccdde0eab352b5f1ce2e8211.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ n(\\sqrt{2} + 1)\\qquad  \\textbf{(B)}\\ n(\\sqrt{2} - 1)\\qquad  \\textbf{(C)}\\ n\\qquad  \\textbf{(D)}\\ n(2 - \\sqrt{2})\\qquad  \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{n\\pi}{\\sqrt{2} + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"614\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1958_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the new circle has twice the area of the original circle, its radius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" /> times the old radius. \nThus, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/a/38a95ad1b0b19e8d52644cd0ff4a5306096f1cbc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r + n = r\\sqrt{2}\\]\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/3/35345cf545001faecf14fed200491db39d34c19e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = r\\sqrt{2} - r\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/e/46e0cbdbb3f4c9c42cb06a9e7af2ce9761aad6e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = r(\\sqrt{2} - 1)\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f20b3a5424b38a52436ad02c48b10c65d5ca6af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r = \\frac{n}{\\sqrt{2} - 1}\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"37\" />\nRationalizing the denominator yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/8/85862773da08a3512a5251f9f4bdbd3b9356de09.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r = \\frac{n}{\\sqrt{2} - 1} *  \\frac{\\sqrt{2} + 1}{\\sqrt{2} + 1} = n(\\sqrt{2} + 1)\\]\" width=\"272\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/5/815b035c9b1a5be0bed175652839987406063483.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"37\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1958_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1958_AHSME\" title=\"1958 AHSME\">1958 AHSC</a>